  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive ({他動詞|たどうし}). No intransitive pair.\n\nUSAGE:\nThis verb is specific to preparing tea, especially {抹茶|まっちゃ}. It is not used for brewing other beverages. For making regular tea ({煎茶|せんちゃ} etc.), use {入|い}れる or {淹|い}れる instead.\n\nThe polite form お{茶|ちゃ}を{点|た}てる is very common, reflecting the formality associated with {茶道|さどう} (tea ceremony).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {抹茶|まっちゃ}を{点|た}てる: to make matcha\n- お{茶|ちゃ}を{点|た}てる: to make tea (polite)\n- {薄茶|うすちゃ}を{点|た}てる: to make thin tea\n- {濃茶|こいちゃ}を{点|た}てる: to make thick tea",
